ur  programmers at link are are setting up a  system so that the part of speech will  be identified if you save a word okay  this is an adjective that helps a lot  but after a while that just gets blended  into  this gradual absorption absorption of  the language  and and an increasing familiarity with  how the language works  and eventually you don't need to worry  about  particles and if you do have  a moment of uncertainty about which  particle to use you can google and you  can find umpteen explanations so  sure if you're interested in looking up  japanese particles you can find lots  better explanations than i gave you just  now however fundamentally to become  comfortable in using japanese particles  or the subjunctive in spanish or  you know prepositions and or pronouns in  italian you just have to expose yourself  to a lot of the language there is no  shortcut in my view so there you have it  i may not be tremendously helpful but i  would encourage learners of japanese not  to focus too much  on the bits and pieces but to make sure  they expose themselves to as much  interesting compelling content as  possible thank you for listening bye for  now  [Music]  you
 

